API.txtx
lab for TAC-368

Find an API that interests you and write an app that 
interacts with it.  At a minimum, you should be able
to send it some piece of key information and have it
send you some information back.  Display
the interaction of course.

Example: weather, send it zip code, it send temperature
and wind speed_direction.  

But do not do the weather one.  I am giving you that one.
Do something besides the weather.

Example: send a stock code and it sends you the current
share price.  

Some APIs provide a list of things as a start, and you
pick one to dig deeper.  

And I know that some of you have done this API fetch thing
in other languages, so the point is not about the API,
but how to handle the calls and returns in Flutter.

The site https://dev.to/onlyoneerin/
38-awesome-apis-to-inspire-your-next-software-project-4395
has lots of possibilities.  Or find one on your own.

We may demo these for the class (20261 after break).  